--[[
    MANA MM2 — Murder Mystery 2
    UI: Obsidian (deividcomsono)
    Key: R/SCRIPTS2026

    dump notes (what this is built on):
      - no anticheat listed.
      - roles: Remotes.Gameplay.GetCurrentPlayerData (InvokeServer) + PlayerDataChanged / RoundStart (OnClientEvent)
        give a table keyed by player name: { Role = "Murderer"|"Sheriff"|"Hero"|"Innocent", Dead, Knife, Gun, Perk }
        the client already receives every role (CurrentRoundClient.GetMurdererPerk scans it).
      - weapons: Tool tagged "Weapon_Knife" / "Weapon_Gun" (CollectionService, replicated).
      - coins: <Map>.CoinContainer.Coin_Server parts, attrs CoinID + Collected.
        CoinCollected(coinId, current, max) -> bag full when max <= current; CoinsStarted resets.
      - aiming: ClientServices.WeaponService.GetMouseTargetCFrame / GetTargetPosition turn the mouse into the
        world point weapons aim at. zero callers in the 268 dumped scripts -> their callers are the Gun/Knife
        tool scripts the dumper skipped. silent aim replaces those two module fields.
      - emotes: Remotes.Misc.PlayEmote is a BindableEvent. Animate's handler plays any Sync.Emotes key with no
        ownership check (only the /e chat path checks ProfileData.Emotes.Owned), and Animate loads every emote.
        your own character's animations replicate, so others see them.
      - NOT in this dump (verify live): the dropped gun's name ("GunDrop", the long-standing MM2 name) and
        whether the knife registers firetouchinterest touches (kill aura).
]]

